     {
      "text": "是 A 还是 B？",
      "tr": "is it A or B?"
     },
     {
      "text": "还是 … 吧",
      "tr": "had better …"
     }
    ],
    "phrases": [],
    "synonyms": [
     {
      "word": "或者",
      "register": "neutral",
      "nuance": "huòzhě: ‘or’ in statements — not for asking someone to choose"
     },
     {
      "word": "要么",
      "register": "colloquial",
      "nuance": "yàome: ‘either … or …’ (要么 A，要么 B) — two options, pick one"
     }
    ],
    "etymology": {
     "text": "还 ‘still; also’ + 是 ‘to be’.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "German oder, Greek ή and Russian или cover every ‘or’; Chinese has two: 还是 asks (‘tea or coffee?’), 或者 states (‘tea or coffee, either is fine’)."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "A 还是 question needs no 吗: 你喝茶还是咖啡？ (not *…咖啡吗？).",
     "In a statement ‘or’ is 或者: 我喝茶或者咖啡."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "还 is read hái here; the same character is huán in 还 ‘to give back’."
    ]
   }
