    "etymology": {
     "text": "或 ‘some, someone; perhaps’ (Schuessler: from 有 ‘there is’ with a distributive suffix) + the suffix 者.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Two Chinese ‘or’s for one German oder: 或者 for statements, 还是 for questions of choice."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
